#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:1
msgid "uniq"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:3
msgid "Removes all duplicates from an array in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:5
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:7
msgid "First install using npm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:11
msgid "Then use it as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:26
msgid "`require(\"uniq\")(array[, compare, sorted])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:27
msgid "Removes all duplicates from a sorted array in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:29
msgid "`array` is the array to remove items from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:30
msgid ""
"`compare` is an optional comparison function that returns 0 when two "
"items are equal, and something non-zero when they are different.  If "
"unspecified, then the default equals will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:31
msgid "`sorted` if true, then assume array is already sorted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:33
msgid "**Returns:** A reference to `array`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:35
msgid ""
"**Time Complexity:** `O(array.length * log(arra.length))` or "
"`O(array.length)` if `sorted`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:38
msgid "Why use this instead of underscore.uniq[ue]?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:39
msgid "A few reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:41
msgid ""
"This library updates the array in place without making an extra copy (and"
" so it is faster for large arrays)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:42
msgid ""
"It also accepts a custom comparison function so you can remove duplicates"
" from arrays containing object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/uniq_README.md:43
msgid ""
"It is more modular in the sense that it doesn't come with a bazillion "
"other utility grab bag functions."
msgstr ""

